In article <97@rc6.urc.tue.nl> wsbucan@eutws1.win.tue.nl (Boudewijn Wayers) writes:
>I don't think one should be able to recharge magic lamps.
>Recharging these lamps is illogic, since the "charge" is in fact
>a djinny (SP?), that is released when the lamp is rubbed. Since
>the djinny gives you a wish, and not the lamp, a magic lamp should
>be one-use only.
>
>Anyone care to comment?

OK, if you're going to make charges on magic lamps illegal then you should
be able to catch a tame djinn with an empty magic lamp.

1)  Obtain empty magic lamp.

2)  Summon djinn.

3)  Charm djinn.

4)  Standing next to djinn, apply magic lamp to djinn.  This might work
    on a sleeping or stunned angry djinn as well.

Yield: a magic lamp (1)

Once a djinn has granted the wish he should dissappear, as otherwise
it would be too easy to recapture him.

There should be a chance that the djinn will resist at the last minute,
destroying the lamp and becoming *especially* angry (2X normal speed).
Note - a djinn might be angry upon being released, but imagine his anger
at escaping entrapment and then standing before the one who tried to trap
him.

Attempting to capture a djinn in a normal lamp should work for 2-3 turns,
at which time the *especially* angry djinn breaks out and says "foolish
mortal, you thought a normal lamp could hold me?" just before wreaking
havok upon your body.

Attempting to capture a djinn in a magic lamp that already contains a djinn
should work for 2-3 turns, at which time *both* djinns break out, destroying
the lamp, and then your poor bod.

How about alignment?  If a chaotic djinn is released (by your rubbing) from
a blessed lamp he will be in a foul mood.  However, the cursed lamp (matching
his alignment) will release him in a good mood.  How do you know what its
alignment will be?  You don't, unless you put the djinn in there in the first
place.

It might be very difficult to capture a chaotic djinn with a blessed lamp;
the tame chaotic djinn might jump around to escape the applied lamp if it
is blessed.  This would wake up a djinn that was sleeping (Applying a lamp
with the opposite status to the djinn).

This means that it would be dangerous to automatically bless a magic lamp
that you discovered with a djinn inside.  Since you wouldn't know the djinn's
alignment, your blessing of the lamp could turn the djinn against you.
